<!--
    The Versio mark, drawn in the app rather than only in the .ico.

    The shell showed the word "Versio" in accent blue and nothing else, while the real mark -
    assets/versio.svg, two plates and an agreement disc - existed and appeared nowhere a user
    could see it. This is that drawing, at 20 px, in the app's own colours.

    THREE PLACES CARRY THIS GEOMETRY, and the header of assets/versio.svg says so: the SVG
    reference drawing, tools/New-VersioIcon.ps1 which redraws it per icon size, and here.
    Change one, change all three.

    Two departures from the SVG, both deliberate:

    - NO TILE. The rounded #1D2026 square is what makes an icon readable against an unknown
      desktop; inside a bar that is already Surface.Base it would be an invisible square with
      a visible edge.
    - The badge is punched in Surface.Base rather than the tile colour, for the same reason:
      the notch has to be the colour of whatever the mark is sitting on.

    A ControlTemplate rather than a DrawingImage, and that is not a style preference. A
    Freezable in a resource dictionary resolves its DynamicResource once and is not re-resolved
    when the palette underneath it is replaced - the exact trap ThemeManager.cs documents at
    length. A template is instantiated per use and resolves its brushes there, so the mark
    follows a theme switch like every other control does.
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <ControlTemplate x:Key="BrandMark" TargetType="ContentControl">
        <!-- Drawn at the SVG's 64-unit scale and scaled by the Viewbox, so the numbers here
             can be compared with the reference drawing without arithmetic. -->
        <Viewbox Stretch="Uniform">
            <Canvas Width="64" Height="64">

                <!-- Mirror on top, project below, equal weight. The disc sits in the gap
                     and notches both: the two sides currently agree. -->
                <Border Canvas.Left="13" Canvas.Top="15" Width="38" Height="14"
                        CornerRadius="4"
                        Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Text.Primary}" />
                <Border Canvas.Left="13" Canvas.Top="35" Width="38" Height="14"
                        CornerRadius="4"
                        Background="{DynamicResource Brush.Text.Disabled}" />

                <!-- The notch, then the badge inside it. 32,32 / r 8.5 and 6 in the SVG. -->
                <Ellipse Canvas.Left="23.5" Canvas.Top="23.5" Width="17" Height="17"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource Brush.Surface.Base}" />
                <Ellipse Canvas.Left="26" Canvas.Top="26" Width="12" Height="12"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource Brush.Status.Added}" />
            </Canvas>
        </Viewbox>
    </ControlTemplate>

</ResourceDictionary>
